# Public build settings. Nothing here is a secret: all four are baked into the bundle.
# Copy to `.env` (git-ignored) and leave a pair out to keep that feature in demo mode.

# ── Telegram deep links (share + «دعوت هم‌رزم») ─────────────────────────────────
# Leave empty for a build without bot settings: links then point at the page itself with
# ?startapp=…, which works in a normal browser and for local testing.
# VITE_TG_BOT: the bot's username — `YourBot`, `@YourBot` or `https://t.me/YourBot` all work.
# VITE_TG_APP: the Mini App's short name from BotFather. Optional; without it links open the bot's
#              Main Mini App. A full `https://t.me/YourBot/YourApp` in either variable sets both.
VITE_TG_BOT=
VITE_TG_APP=

# ── Telegram sign-in + real teams (Supabase Edge Function `game-auth`) ───────────
# Without the endpoint the game stays the local demo: playable, simulated team, web invite links.
# VITE_GAME_API_URL: https://<project-ref>.supabase.co/functions/v1/game-auth
# VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY: the project's anon (publishable) key — public by design; it only opens
#   the function gateway, and the function verifies Telegram initData before touching the database.
VITE_GAME_API_URL=
VITE_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=
